# Source files are TEXT, whatever their bytes happen to look like.
#
# Git classifies a file as binary when it finds a NUL in the first 8000 bytes. A single
# unescaped control character inside a string literal is enough — and PR #122 shipped exactly
# that: `terrarium-decode.spec.ts` carried one raw NUL while testing a PNG chunk name, so git
# rendered the file as `Binary files … differ` and the only spec guarding the hand-written
# decoder's untrusted-input refusals became invisible to every diff review, on GitHub and in
# `git diff` alike (review #122, CODE122-I1 / TA122-I1).
#
# The escape was restored at the source, which fixes that file. This attribute is the belt: it
# stops the same accident from silently reclassifying any future source file. `diff` forces a
# textual diff even where the heuristic would refuse one, so a reviewer always sees lines.
*.ts text diff
*.mjs text diff
*.js text diff
*.json text diff
*.md text diff
